    <section id="sobre">

        <h2>About Us</h2>

        <h3>Bruno</h3>

        <h4>Birth</h4>

        <p>
            My name is Bruno Henrique Blodorn. I was born on January 31, 2011, in Toledo, 
            at Centro Hospitalar do Oeste Ltda., weighing 1.567 kg. I was eagerly awaited by my 
            entire family; I am Camile's twin brother and the youngest sibling in the family.
        </p>


        <h4>Educational Background</h4>

        <p>
            Since I was little, I have always studied in Maripá. My early years were spent at 
            Escola Municipal Professor Leopoldo Kuroli, where I studied up to the 5th grade. 
            Afterward, I went to Colégio Estadual PIO XII, where I completed my Elementary and 
            Middle School education. Currently, I am attending High School at IFPR (Federal Institute 
            of Paraná) in Toledo.
        </p>


        <h4>Historical Fact:</h4>

        <p>
            In 2011, the official release of Minecraft took place, becoming one of the most famous 
            games in the world. The full version of the game was launched on November 18, 2011, during 
            MineCon, after going through a period of development and test versions. The game stood 
            out for allowing players to explore, build, and create their own worlds using blocks. 
            Since then, Minecraft has become a global phenomenon and continues to be updated and 
            played by millions of people.
        </p>


        <h4>Current Moment:</h4>

        <p>
            Currently, I am studying at the Federal Institute of Paraná (IFPR) in Toledo, where 
            I have made several special friendships and am gaining knowledge in various fields, 
            especially technology.
        </p>


        <h4>Future Perspectives:</h4>

        <p>
            I would like to go to college in the field of Communication, and if that doesn't 
            work out, I plan to take the entrance exam to become an Army Officer.
        </p>

