    <section id="onde-vivemos">

        <h2>Where Do We Live?</h2>

        <h4>Municipality - Maripá:</h4>

        <p>
            It originated on May 13, 1946, with the founding of Companhia Madeireira Rio Paraná S/A 
            (MARIPÁ), and was emancipated from Palotina by State Law No. 9,226 on April 17, 1990. 
            Maripá is well known for its festivals, the "Orchid Festival" (Festa das Orquídeas) and 
            the "Tractor Drag Race" (Arrancadão de Tratores), attracting visitors from all over Brazil 
            and other countries. Maripá is also appreciated for its agriculture and fertile soil.
        </p>


        <h4>Rural Community (Linha):</h4>

        <p>
            It is connected to the colonization and agricultural settlement process that began in the 
            mid-20th century, characterized by the division of small rural properties and a strong 
            presence of family farming and dairy cattle ranching.
        </p>

